"p\",\".$.$.2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\".$.$.0\",{\"children\":\"BYOK:\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}],\" the provider bills you for inference directly. Standard and Business include \",\"$L7f\",\" of list-price inference per month through BYOK with no OpenRouter fee; Enterprise includes \",\"$L80\",\". Above the allowance, OpenRouter charges 5% of what the same request would cost at list price on OpenRouter, deducted from your credits.\"],\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}]],\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}]\n47:[\"No. An attempt that errors is not charged for its model tokens, so with fallback you pay only for the run that answers. Under\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",\".$.$.2\",{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors text-xs cursor-pointer\",\"href\":\"https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/features/zero-completion-insurance\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[false,\"Zero Completion Insurance\",null]}],\" \",\"the same holds for a response that returns nothing and no finish reason; auxiliary services that already ran, such as web search or file parsing, may still be billed. Routing through openrouter/auto adds no fee; you pay the rate of whichever model serves the request.\"]\n72:[\"OpenRouter sets no plan-based rate limit on paid models. A limit you hit there normally comes from the provider, and fallback routing retries other providers automatically; only very high burst traffic is rejected by OpenRouter's own DDoS protection with a 429. Free models are capped at 20 requests per minute and 50 per day, rising to 1,000 per day once your account has bought at least $10 of credits. Failed attempts count toward that daily cap, and a negative balance blocks free models until you add credits. Details are in the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",\".$.$.2\",{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors text-xs cursor-pointer\",\"href\":\"/docs/api_reference/limits\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[false,\"rate limits documentation\",null]}],\".\"]\n73:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-col gap-y-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\".$.$.0\",{\"children\":\"If a model is deprecated, you will receive a 404 when you request it, with an error message like \\\"no endpoints for this model found.\\\"\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",\".$.$.1\",{\"children\":\"If the pricing changes, we will continue to route to the model and it will serve your requests. But, you will be charged at the new rate and your credits will deduct accordingly. This will be reflected in your billing.\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}]],\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}]\n74:[\"Our API is OpenAI‑compatible. Update the base URL and model names; see\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L7e\",\".$.$.2\",{\"href\":\"/docs/quickstart\",\"children\":\"Quickstart\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}],\".\"]\n75:[\"Routing/fallback can automatically try alternative models, and an attempt that errors is not charged for its model tokens under\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",\".$.$.2\",{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors text-xs cursor-pointer\",\"href\":\"https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/features/zero-completion-insurance\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[false,\"Zero Completion Insurance\",null]}],\".\"]\n76:[\"Visit the \",[\"$\",\"a\",\".$.$.1\",{\"className\":\"text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 decoration-current/40 hover:text-accent-foreground hover:decoration-current transition-colors text-xs cursor-pointer\",\"href\":\"https://status.openrouter.ai/\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[false,\"status\",null]}],\" \",\"page for real‑time uptime and incident history.\"]\n77:\"404: Not Found\"\n78:\"Go Home\"\n79:\"Browse Models\"\n19: